# Files the sdist carries beyond what setuptools finds on its own.
#
# setuptools already includes README.md, LICENSE, pyproject.toml and the package
# sources. Everything else at the repository root is dropped silently, which is
# how SKILL.md and the four translated READMEs would ship with the repository but
# not with the distribution - and a `pip download --no-binary` user would get
# documentation that stops at one language and no skill at all.
#
# The wheel is deliberately untouched: it carries the importable package and
# nothing else. Nothing in `laya_mcp` reads SKILL.md, so this changes what a
# source consumer can read, not what the installed package can do.

include SKILL.md
include README.md
include README-zh.md
include README-es.md
include README-pt.md
include README-hi.md
